<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!-- ====================================================================
       ORBIT LAYER SIZE

       Odyssey's orbit layer is generated as an icosphere with HALF the
       subdivision depth of the planet surface:

           Core   Surface : radius 100, subdivisions 10
           Odyssey Orbit  : radius 130, subdivisions 5

       Tile count scales with ~4^subdivisions, so orbit has orders of
       magnitude fewer tiles than the surface. Since PlanetLayerDef.Orbit
       sets settlementsPer100kTiles to 1000~1000 (one settlement per ~100
       tiles), a small tile count also means very few orbital settlements,
       asteroids and points of interest.

       Raising subdivisions by 1 multiplies tile count by roughly 4, and
       scales settlements/sites/travel distance with it.

       COST: worldgen time and orbit mesh vertex count grow with the same
       factor. 5 -> 6 is the conservative step. 7 is a 16x jump; try it only
       after confirming 6 generates in acceptable time.

       MULTIPLAYER: this is a def, so both clients get an identical value
       as long as they run the same mod version.
       ==================================================================== -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>/Defs/PlanetLayerSettingsDef[defName="Orbit"]/settings/subdivisions</xpath>
    <value>
      <subdivisions>6</subdivisions>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
